  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0">Read both notes files and design 5.1/5.1a/5.1c. Verify against live metadata: `sprk_containerid` type, `ownerid` is an OWNER field, and that a business unit named per the configured value exists in dev.</step>
    <step order="1">Add configuration for the BU name (default "Secure Projects") and a resolver that looks it up by name, selecting $top=2 so ambiguity is detectable. Fail closed with a reason code on absent or ambiguous.</step>
    <step order="2">Delete Step 2 (BU creation), Step 4 (account creation), their rollback paths, `ResolveRootBusinessUnitIdAsync`, `ResolveAccountForBuAsync`, and the now-dead response/request fields. Keep the response honest about what it actually did.</step>
    <step order="3">Assign the project's owner to the resolved BU's default owner team. Confirm from live metadata how that team is identified, and verify a team assignment actually succeeds rather than assuming.</step>
    <step order="4">Reduce the Step 5 stamp to `sprk_containerid` only -- a plain string write. Comment that no navigation property is involved and why.</step>
    <step order="5">Fix the idempotency marker so it keys only on state provisioning writes. Comment why `sprk_containerid` is unsuitable.</step>
    <step order="6">Replace the swallow with a fail-loud path: non-2xx, a reason code, and the created container id for reconciliation.</step>
    <step order="7">Author tests: BU resolved by name; absent BU fails closed; ambiguous BU fails closed; owner set to the team; container stamped; a failed stamp returns non-2xx carrying the container id; provisioning NEVER writes sprk_externalaccount; a wizard-cascaded container id does NOT trigger the already-provisioned 409.</step>
    <step order="8">Perturb: fall back to the root BU on absent; revert the marker to `sprk_containerid`; re-swallow the stamp failure; write `sprk_externalaccount`; skip the owner assignment. Record counts.</step>
    <step order="9">Amend spec.md FR-18/FR-28 acceptance criteria if they still describe the old mechanism. Full suite (all SEVEN test projects); publish size; notes; update TASK-INDEX.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If assigning a record to the BU's default owner team fails because the team lacks entity privileges, STOP and escalate -- that is the `Secure Project Owner` role dependency (design 5.1a), which is environment setup and not this task's to create. Report exactly what Dataverse refused.</trigger>
    <trigger>If no business unit matching the configured name exists in the target environment, STOP -- do not create one. That is environment setup, and creating it here would reintroduce exactly the behaviour this task removes.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>ProvisionProjectEndpoint already resolves BUs, creates containers and PATCHes the project. This task removes two of its steps and corrects the other two.</existing>
    <extension>Net deletion. One configuration key and one name-based resolver replace a creation path plus two resolvers.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Secure-project provisioning currently 409s for any user whose BU carries a container id, so no secure project is provisioned at all. When it did run it created a per-project BU outside the BU that NFR-05 guards, plus an account nothing reads -- and repairing the stamp as originally specified would overwrite each project's CLIENT with a synthetic account.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/ExternalAccess/ProvisionProjectEndpoint.cs</output>
    <output type="test">tests/integration/auth/UnifiedAccessControl/ProvisionSecureProjectTests.cs</output>
    <output type="spec">projects/unified-access-control-r2/spec.md</output>
    <output type="doc">projects/unified-access-control-r2/notes/task-021-provisioning-stamping.md</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion>No business unit is created by provisioning under any code path.</criterion>
    <criterion>No account is created, and `sprk_externalaccount` is never present in any write payload -- pinned by a test that fails if it appears.</criterion>
    <criterion>The Secure Projects BU is resolved by NAME from configuration; an absent or ambiguous match fails closed with a reason code and never falls back to the root or caller BU.</criterion>
    <criterion>The project's owner is the resolved BU's default owner team, verified by reading the owner back.</criterion>
    <criterion>The stamp writes `sprk_containerid` only, as a plain string with no `@odata.bind`.</criterion>
    <criterion>A stamp failure returns non-2xx carrying a reason code and the created container id.</criterion>
    <criterion>A project carrying a wizard-cascaded `sprk_containerid` is still provisionable -- the live 409 regression is closed, proven by a test.</criterion>
    <criterion>Every perturbation in step 8 fails at least one test; counts recorded in the notes file.</criterion>
    <criterion>All 7 test projects pass; publish size reported and &lt;=60 MB compressed incl. PDBs.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>RE-SCOPED 2026-08-25. The original "fix 3 wrong names" scope would have activated a data-corruption bug. The nav-property blocker that stopped the first attempt dissolves here because the only remaining stamped field is plain text. Document isolation is NOT achieved by this task -- nothing reads the project's container yet; that is `spaarke-secure-project-r1`.</notes>
</task>
